  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> be a point on the <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis. Common tangents are drawn from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> to the curves <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>x</mi></math>. If one of these tangents touches the two curves at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is equal to"
  },
